The diff introduces new nontrivial logic in `pkg/plugins/log/logger.go`:

```go
func (d *grafanaInfraLogWrapper) FromContext(ctx context.Context) Logger {
  concreteInfraLogger, ok := d.l.FromContext(ctx).(*log.ConcreteLogger)
  if !ok {
    return d.New()
  }
  return &grafanaInfraLogWrapper{ l: concreteInfraLogger }
}
```

There are no corresponding tests added/updated in the diff to cover the `!ok` branch. The fallback behavior (`return d.New()`) is silent and, as written, does not use `ctx`, so any contextual attributes intended to be derived from the context would not be applied in that branch. This is a concrete, diff-grounded edge-case/testing gap rather than a clearly demonstrated functional defect in the normal path.
